## 10. Salary-slip email delivery

Generate and send a separate email to each employee.

Never put multiple employees in To, CC or BCC on the same salary email.

Email recipient:

- The active staff profile’s approved email address

Suggested subject:

`Topclues Solutions Salary Slip – [MMMM YYYY] – [Employee Full Name]`

Email body should include:

- Employee name
- Salary month
- Confirmation that the salary slip is available
- Secure portal link
- Contact-HR message
- Company signature

Attach the correct employee PDF when supported and also provide an authenticated portal link.

Email requirements:

- Send from a backend function, never directly from the browser.
- Store SMTP, Gmail or API credentials only in Secret Manager.
- Make the email provider configurable.
- Support Firebase Trigger Email, authenticated Gmail API or SMTP through a clean provider adapter.
- Use an idempotency key containing staff ID, payroll period and salary-slip version.
- Prevent accidental duplicate emails.
- Track Pending, Processing, Sent and Failed status.
- Store provider message ID, attempt count, last attempt, sent time and safe error summary.
- Allow Admin/HR to retry failed messages.
- Display batch progress and a final delivery report.
- Require a confirmation screen before batch sending.
- Never include complete bank information in the email.
- Create an audit event for each send and retry.
- Do not let a client write arbitrary recipients or arbitrary email contents into the email queue.

